{{also|milch}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|miluh|lang=goh}} (akin to {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|miluk|lang=osx}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*meluks}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₂melǵ-}}. Compare {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|mælk|lang=da}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|melk|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|fy|-}} {{term|molke|lang=fy}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|melk|lang=no}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|meolc|lang=ang}}, English {{term|milk|lang=en}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|mjölk|lang=sv}}, {{etyl|yi|-}} {{term|מילך|sc=Hebr|tr=milkh|lang=yi}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/mɪlç/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Milch.ogg|audio (Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-Milch.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Milchen|pl2=Milche}}

# [[milk]]; white liquid produced by female animals for their young to drink
# a [[white]] [[fluid]] that is [[exuded]] by certain [[plants]]
# a [[white]] [[liquid]] that is a [[mixture]] of other [[substances]], where one of the components is very finely distributed
# the white [[semen]] of a male [[fish]]

